            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0651" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg557"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.12155/459: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul at Ciudad Judrez</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Blocker</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-10T14:00:00-04:00">September 10, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Please deliver following message to Boundary Commissioner Lawson: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Reference telegram No. 208, September 9, 4 p.m. from American Embassy,
                            Mexico City, to Department copy of which is stated to have been sent to
                            you by airmail. Reference also to draft Minute referred to in
                            telegram.</p>
                        <p>When you have received draft Minute please consult with Mexican
                            Commissioner Serrano and send your observations thereon to the
                            Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
